    <strong>Privacy &amp; Terms</strong><br><br>
  LifeTold is a personal memoir companion that helps you record, organise and preserve your life story. By continuing you agree to the following:<br><br>
  <em>The short version: your stories and photos are yours. LifeTold uses AI to help write them, and some of that processing happens overseas (see clause 1). You are responsible for what you add about other people and what you choose to share. Premium is optional and you can cancel any time. You can delete your account whenever you like.</em><br><br>
  <strong>1. Third-Party AI Processing &amp; Overseas Data Transfer.</strong> To generate stories, check for duplicate entries, and assist with writing, your memoir content is sent overseas for AI processing. For all plans, free and Premium, content is sent to <strong>Anthropic, Inc.</strong> (United States) via their API. If Anthropic is temporarily unavailable, requests automatically fail over to <strong>Groq, Inc.</strong> (United States), configured with zero data retention enabled. Voice playback and transcription use <strong>Microsoft Azure AI Speech</strong> (international), which processes audio in server memory only with no data retained at rest. Voice cloning is a separate, optional feature that uses <strong>Inworld AI, Inc.</strong> (United States) — see Settings for details. If you choose to receive optional story prompt emails, your email address and the text of each email are sent via <strong>Resend, Inc.</strong> (United States), which delivers them &mdash; see <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Resend&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>. If you buy Premium or a gift, payment is handled by <strong>Stripe</strong>, which receives your name, email address and payment details; we do not see or store your card number. <em>These providers may process data outside Australia. Australian Privacy Law (including the Australian Privacy Act 1988) may not apply to your information once it is disclosed to these overseas recipients.</em> Anthropic deletes content sent through its API within 30 days, and may keep it longer only where the law or its safety rules require. Under the terms we use, none of these providers uses your content to train its AI models. See <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Anthropic&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://groq.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Groq&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Microsoft&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>, and <a href="https://inworld.ai/privacy" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Inworld&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>. By continuing, you expressly consent to this cross-border disclosure under APP 8.2(a) of the Australian Privacy Act 1988.<br><br>
  <strong>2. Data Storage.</strong> Your entries, photos and account data are stored securely in Australia via <strong>Supabase</strong> (Sydney region, ap-southeast-2) 🇦🇺. See <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">Supabase&rsquo;s Privacy Policy</a>.<br><br>
  <strong>3. Your account.</strong> You sign in with your Google, Apple or Facebook account. You must be 18 or older. Keep your sign-in secure and tell us if you think someone else has used your account. You are responsible for what happens under it.<br><br>
  <strong>4. Your stories and photos.</strong> Everything you write, record or upload stays yours. You give us permission to store it, process it (including with the AI providers in clause 1) and show it to the people you choose to share it with, only so that we can run LifeTold for you. We do not use your content to train AI models and we do not sell it. Only add things you have the right to use.<br><br>
  <strong>5. Family Trees and Other People.</strong> If you add relatives or other people to your family tree, stories or photos, you are responsible for what you add about them. Keep it to what you would be comfortable telling them about. Do not add information about someone in order to harass, expose or harm them, and if a person asks you to remove their information, please do. If you share a family tree link, anyone with the link can see what it shows, and a person who imports a copy keeps that copy even if you later delete the link or your account. Stories and notes are not included when a tree is imported.<br><br>
  <strong>6. AI Writing and Voices.</strong> Gethro and the story drafts are written by AI. They can be wrong, repeat themselves or mix up facts, so please read and correct what it writes before you rely on it or share it. It is not professional, legal, medical or financial advice. Voice cloning is optional: only record a voice if you are that person or they have agreed.<br><br>
  <strong>7. Sharing.</strong> When you share a link, anyone who has it can open it without signing in, and we cannot tell who they are. Only share links with people you trust, and revoke a link in the Sharing panel if you no longer want it to work. You are responsible for what you choose to share. Shared links also stop working while your Premium is not active, and work again when you renew. A copy of a family tree that someone has already imported cannot be taken back (see clause 5).<br><br>
  <strong>8. Using LifeTold Properly.</strong> Do not use LifeTold to break the law, to harass or harm others, to upload content that is unlawful or abusive, to get around its limits or security, or to copy it, reverse engineer it or overload it. We may limit, suspend or end an account that does this, and we will tell you why where we can.<br><br>
  <strong>9. Premium, Payments and Gifts.</strong> Premium is optional. It is a monthly subscription at the price shown at checkout (in Australian dollars unless it says otherwise), and payment is handled by Stripe. It renews each month until you cancel, and cancelling stops future charges. When Premium ends you move to the free plan, and Premium features, including shared links, stop working until you renew. We do not usually refund part of a month that has already been paid for, but if something went wrong with a payment or with the service, contact us and we will put it right. A gift gives the person who claims it one year of Premium, counted from the day they claim it. A gift code that is not claimed expires 12 months after it was bought. If you bought a gift that has not been claimed, contact us and we will refund it. We may cancel a gift if the payment is reversed or refunded.<br><br>
  <strong>10. Data Care.</strong> We take reasonable care to protect your data but cannot guarantee against loss in the event of a technical failure. We recommend exporting your entries periodically.<br><br>
  <strong>11. Your Consumer Rights and Our Liability.</strong> Nothing in these terms limits any right or remedy you have under the Australian Consumer Law or any other law that cannot be excluded. We provide LifeTold with due care and skill, but we cannot promise it will always be available or free of errors. Subject to your rights under the law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss caused by events outside our reasonable control.<br><br>
  <strong>12. Ending Your Account, and If LifeTold Closes.</strong> You can delete your account at any time in the app, which deletes your data as described in the Privacy Policy. If we suspend or end your account for breaking these terms, we will tell you and, where we can, let you export your data first. If we ever decide to close LifeTold, we will give you at least 90 days' notice by email and in the app, give you a way to export your stories as text or PDF, and refund any Premium time or gift you have paid for but not used.<br><br>
  <strong>13. Changes to Terms.</strong> We may update these terms from time to time. You will be asked to re-accept any material changes before continuing.<br><br>
  <strong>14. Privacy, Contact and Governing Law.</strong> Our Privacy Policy at <a href="https://lifetold.app/privacy" target="_blank" style="color:var(--gold-dark)">lifetold.app/privacy</a> explains how we handle your personal information, your rights, and how to make a complaint. To contact us, use Help, then Get in touch, in the app. These terms are governed by the laws of Victoria, Australia, and the courts there can hear disputes about them, without limiting your rights under the Australian Consumer Law.<br><br>
